cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PUMA Analyzer in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "PUMA Analyzer"
abstract: >-
  A Windows desktop application that estimates thin-film thickness and
  optical constants (refractive index n, extinction coefficient k) from
  a measured transmission spectrum, using a physics-based transmittance
  model and a compiled C nonlinear-optimization engine.
